    {
      "id": "a1_u10_l01",
      "level": "A1",
      "unit": 10,
      "title": "Au restaurant",
      "description": "Reserve a table, order your meal and ask for the bill.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 13,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "Getting a table",
              "body": "To book, say \"Je voudrais réserver une table pour deux personnes\" (I would like to reserve a table for two). When you arrive, simply say \"Une table pour deux, s'il vous plaît.\"",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Je voudrais réserver une table pour deux personnes.", "english": "I would like to reserve a table for two people." },
                { "french": "Une table pour quatre, s'il vous plaît.", "english": "A table for four, please." },
                { "french": "Vous avez réservé ?", "english": "Do you have a reservation?" },
                { "french": "Vous avez une table pour ce soir ?", "english": "Do you have a table for tonight?" },
                { "french": "Nous sommes trois.", "english": "There are three of us." }
              ]
            },
            {
              "heading": "Ordering and paying",
              "body": "The waiter brings \"la carte\" (the menu). Careful: in French, \"le menu\" usually means a fixed-price set of dishes! To order, say \"Je vais prendre...\" (I'll have...). At the end, ask for \"l'addition\" — the bill.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Je vais prendre le poulet.", "english": "I'll have the chicken." },
                { "french": "Et comme boisson ?", "english": "And to drink?", "note": "the waiter's question" },
                { "french": "L'addition, s'il vous plaît !", "english": "The bill, please!" },
                { "french": "Comme entrée, je vais prendre la salade.", "english": "As a starter, I'll have the salad." },
                { "french": "Un verre d'eau, s'il vous plaît.", "english": "A glass of water, please." }
              ],
              "tip": "Service is included in French restaurants — a tip (un pourboire) is appreciated but never required."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
