      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "Talking about the weather",
              "body": "Weather small talk uses \"il fait...\": \"Il fait beau\" (the weather is nice), \"Il fait froid\" (it's cold), \"Il fait chaud\" (it's hot). For rain, say \"Il pleut\" (it's raining). To ask: \"Quel temps fait-il ?\"",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Quel temps fait-il ?", "english": "What's the weather like?" },
                { "french": "Il fait beau aujourd'hui !", "english": "The weather is nice today!" },
                { "french": "Il pleut.", "english": "It's raining." },
                { "french": "Il fait chaud en été.", "english": "It's hot in the summer." },
                { "french": "Il neige en hiver.", "english": "It snows in winter." }
              ],
              "tip": "\"Le temps\" means both \"weather\" and \"time\" — context tells you which one."
            },
            {
              "heading": "Survival phrases",
              "body": "When you don't understand, don't panic! Say \"Je ne comprends pas\" (I don't understand) and ask \"Pouvez-vous répéter, s'il vous plaît ?\" (Can you repeat, please?). \"Parlez plus lentement\" means \"speak more slowly\".",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Excusez-moi, je ne comprends pas.", "english": "Sorry, I don't understand." },
                { "french": "Pouvez-vous répéter, s'il vous plaît ?", "english": "Can you repeat, please?" },
                { "french": "Parlez plus lentement, s'il vous plaît.", "english": "Speak more slowly, please." },
                { "french": "Vous parlez anglais ?", "english": "Do you speak English?" },
                { "french": "Merci beaucoup pour votre aide !", "english": "Thank you very much for your help!" }
              ],
              "tip": "French speakers love it when you try. One little \"Excusez-moi, je ne parle pas bien français\" and they will slow down for you."
            }
          ]
        },
